HW-025  ES8311: an attempt to shorten the six-second ADC wake-up. INCONCLUSIVE.
        Recorded because the negative is worth having and the lever is worth knowing.

        M5Stack StickS3 (3rd unit, COM35), Zephyr 4.4.0, 2026-07-13.

WHY THIS WAS TRIED
------------------
HW-023 established that the ES8311's ADC takes about six seconds of wall clock to wake
up after the codec's analog state is disturbed, that there is no sample-rate dependence,
and that neither the analog bias register (0x10 = 0x1F) nor the power-up stage timers
(0x0B / 0x0C = 0x00) shorten it.

The datasheet (Everest ES8311, Rev 10.0, Jan 2021) explains why none of that was going
to work, and names the one thing that might.

There is NO microphone-bias pin on this codec. Pins 14, 15 and 16 are DACVREF, ADCVREF
and VMID, and the datasheet describes all three identically: "Analog Filtering capacitor
connection". Its own typical application circuit hangs 1 uF on each. So the settling time
is three capacitors charging -- as much a property of the board's component values as of
the chip -- which is exactly why no chip datasheet can specify it, and none does. Neither
does any reference driver: the longest delay anywhere in eight of them is 20 ms, and
mainline Linux's es8311.c says so outright:

    /* Specific delay is not documented, using the same as es8316. */
    usleep_range(5000, 5500);

The 0x00 block reset clears CSM_ON, which powers the state machine and the analog down.
The caps discharge. Charging them back is the six seconds.

And register 0x0D bits [1:0] are VMIDSEL, whose documented values are:

    0 - vmid off        1 - normal speed charge        3 - start up vmid FAST speed charge

A field whose entire purpose is the speed of the thing being measured. All EIGHT
reference drivers -- ESP-ADF, esp_codec_dev, esp-bsp, esp-dev-kits, NuttX, Bouffalo,
mainline Linux and the ANYCUBIC vendor tree -- write 0x0D = 0x01. Normal. So does this
driver. Nobody uses the fast charge.

RESULT
------
    arm                                        woke after   "steady" floor
    A  0x0D as the driver writes it (VMIDSEL=1)   5151 ms        573
    B  VMIDSEL=3, fast speed charge               4128 ms       1404
    C  VMIDSEL=3 + IBIAS_SW level3 (0x10=0x1f)    4641 ms       1003

Read naively, B is a second faster than A and the fast charge works. That reading does
not survive contact with the rest of the data, and this run is recorded as a NEGATIVE for
two reasons.

1. THE RUN-TO-RUN VARIANCE IS AS LARGE AS THE EFFECT. Arm A is the same experiment as
   HW-023c arm A, on the same board, with the same code. HW-023c measured 6175 ms. This
   run measured 5151 ms. That is a one-second spread between two runs of an IDENTICAL
   arm -- the same size as the A-to-B difference the experiment is trying to claim. And
   C, which adds the maximum analog bias on top of the fast charge, came back SLOWER than
   B rather than faster, which an effect this clean should not do.

2. THE METRIC IS CONTAMINATED. The "steady floor" column should read 81..116 -- that is
   this board's settled noise floor, measured many times today. It reads 573, 1404, 1003.
   Those are five to fifteen times too high, which means the peak-RMS-over-500 ms readout
   is being dominated by room noise, not by the codec. If a transient can move the steady
   floor by 10x, it can also trip the >= 40 wake threshold early, and the "woke after"
   column inherits that.

So: no claim is made here. The fast charge is neither confirmed nor refuted.

WHAT WOULD SETTLE IT
--------------------
A median-over-the-window floor instead of a peak, so a cough does not register; each arm
repeated enough times to state a variance rather than a number; and a quiet room. None of
that is hard. It was not done because it does not block anything: the driver does not
reset the codec and does not need to (HW-023d: writing every register it depends on gives
a fully deterministic state at zero settling cost), so the six seconds are only ever paid
on a true cold power-on, by the board, before any driver runs.

The lever is recorded here for whoever wants it. VMIDSEL = 3 is documented, unused by
every reference implementation, and costs one constant.

